    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Selecting the API**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Vision API for image text detection. It seems like a solid, reliable choice for this project and handles a variety of scenarios.\n\n\n**Defining the Framework**\n\nI've outlined the core steps for `detect_image_text.py`. First, Google Cloud Vision AI is chosen as the external provider. Then, I plan to import the `google.cloud.vision` library and implement the text detection using the client, image loading, and the `text_detection` method. Finally, I will write the code to the file. I also plan to add a placeholder to the code.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864395605,
          "start": 1789864392384
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc3b36c0001sYHHMIlZ2IrMwf",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc3b331700177WAkKH76JNBmb",
      "session_id": "ses_f43c4ccf9ffeGKsXdEP4n0u5LR",
      "time_created": 1789864392384,
      "time_updated": 1789864395606
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "JGjlE9GVYhbu7sxZ",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import vision\n\ndef detect_text(image_path_or_uri):\n    \"\"\"Detects text in the image file or at the given URI.\"\"\"\n    client = vision.ImageAnnotatorClient()\n\n    if image_path_or_uri.startswith(\"gs://\") or image_path_or_uri.startswith(\"http://\") or image_path_or_uri.startswith(\"https://\"):\n        image = vision.Image()\n        image.source.image_uri = image_path_or_uri\n    else:\n        with open(image_path_or_uri, 'rb') as image_file:\n            content = image_file.read()\n        image = vision.Image(content=content)\n\n    response = client.text_detection(image=image)\n    texts = response.text_annotations\n\n    if texts:\n        # The first annotation is the overall text detected\n        full_text = texts[0].description\n        print(f\"Full text: {full_text}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No text detected.\")\n\n    for i, text in enumerate(texts[1:], 1):  # Skip the first full text annotation\n        print(f\"Text {i}: {text.description}\")\n        print(f\"Bounds: {','.join([f'{v.x_coordinate},{v.y_coordinate}' for v in text.bounding_poly.vertices])}\")\n\n    if response.error.message:\n        raise Exception(\n            f'{response.error.message}\nFor more info on error messages, check: '\n            f'https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors'\n        )\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Replace with your image path or URI (e.g., \"path/to/your/image.jpg\", \"gs://your-bucket/your-image.jpg\")\n    # Make sure you have authenticated to Google Cloud and enabled the Vision AI API.\n    # For local files, ensure the file exists.\n    # For URIs, ensure public accessibility or appropriate permissions.\n    image_to_process = \"path/to/your/image.jpg\" # Placeholder\n    detect_text(image_to_process)\n",
            "filePath": "detect_image_text.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
