    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Vision AI as the external image description provider. I'm focusing on making this choice explicit and easily identifiable within the `describe_image.py` script, which will be the core of the project.\n\n\n**Defining the `describe_image` Function**\n\nI'm now fleshing out the `describe_image.py` script. The focus is on implementing the `describe_image` function that will interact with Google Cloud Vision AI. I'm importing the `google.cloud.vision_v1` library and outlining how to take an image path as input and retrieve descriptions. My priority is to keep it straightforward and within the specified requirements, avoiding any unnecessary additions. The goal is a concise, functional unit.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864390608,
